t":"Hoekstra","name":"Hoekstra, Pieter J","rank":47,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lea K","key":"davispau","last":"Davis","name":"Davis, Lea K","rank":48,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peristera","key":"paschoupau","last":"Paschou","name":"Paschou, Peristera","rank":49,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36823209"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41398-023-02341-5","issn":["21583188"],"issue":"1","journal":"Translational Psychiatry","paperid":"69","publisher":"Springer Nature","status":"p","title":"Translational Psychiatry","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85148805353"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-a634eb74-aebc-420e-80c5-efdd9e8f456c","ku-c0a5ecd5-42b7-45f1-a6e0-f0a8b2806558"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Polygenic risk score-based phenome-wide association study identifies novel associations for Tourette syndrome","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-085.71-672747","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Growth differentiation factor 15 (GDF15) is a stress signal that can be induced by protein restriction and is associated with reduced food intake. Anorexia of aging, insufficient protein intake as well as high GDF15 concentrations often occur in older age, but it is unknown whether GDF15 concentrations change acutely after meal ingestion and affect appetite in older individuals. After an overnight fast, appetite was assessed in older (n = 20; 73.7 ± 6.30 years) and younger (n = 20; 25.7 ± 4.39 years) women with visual analogue scales, and concentrations of circulating GDF15 and glucagon-like peptide-1 (GLP-1) were quantified before and at 1, 2 and 4 h after ingestion of either dextrose (182 kcal) or a mixed protein-rich meal (450 kcal). In response to dextrose ingestion, appetite increased in both older and younger women, whereas GDF15 concentrations increased only in the older group. In older women, appetite response was negatively correlated with the GDF15 response (rho = -0.802, p = 0.005). Following high-protein ingestion, appetite increased in younger women, but remained low in the old, while GDF15 concentrations did not change significantly in either age group. GLP-1 concentrations did not differ between age groups or test meals. In summary, acute GDF15 response differed between older and younger women. Associations of postprandial appetite and GDF15 following dextrose ingestion in older women suggest a reduced appetite response when the GDF15 response is high, thus supporting the proposed anorectic effects of high GDF15 concentrations.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Herpich, Catrin","Lehmann, Stephanie","Kochlik, Bastian","Kleinert, Maximilian","Klaus, Susanne","Müller-Werdan, Ursula","Norman, Kristina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-491060"],"filters":{"added":"2022-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Charité – Universitätsmedizin Berlin","Evangelisches Geriatriezentrum Berlin","German Center for Diabetes Research","German Centre for Cardiovascular Research","German Institute of Human Nutrition","University of Potsdam"],"keyword":["Adult","Aging","Anorexia of aging","Appetite","Cross Over Studies","Eating","Energy Intake","Female","GDF15","GLP 1","Glucagon Like Peptide 1 blood","Glucose administration dosage","Growth Differentiation Factor 15 blood","Humans","Postprandial Period","Young Adult"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the effect of dextrose or protein ingestion on circulating growth differentiation factor 000000000015 and appetite in older compared to younger women","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/nu14194066","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-491060","identifier":[{"id":"36235718","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC9571024","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85139795344","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-a35f71d0-7b86-47a5-b463-1a08078e8db3"],"keyword":["Adult","Aging","Anorexia of aging","Appetite","Cross-Over Studies","Eating","Energy Intake","Female","GDF15","GLP-1","Glucagon-Like Peptide 1/blood","Glucose/administration & dosage","Growth Differentiation Factor 15/blood","Humans","Postprandial Period","Young Adult"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A8F518E6477B9F72F39E1B2AD736E4A8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/322943261/Herpich_et_al_Nutrients_2022_Vol_14_19_e4066.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/nu14194066","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"university of potsdam","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Potsdam","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"charité universitätsmedizin berlin","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Charité – Universitätsmedizin Berlin","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"german institute of human nutrition","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"German Institute of Human Nutrition","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Nutrition, Exercise and Sports, The August Krogh Section for Molecular Physiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"de","key":"german center for diabetes research","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"German Center for Diabetes Research","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"de","key":"evangelisches geriatriezentrum berlin","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Evangelisches Geriatriezentrum Berlin","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"de","key":"german centre for cardiovascular research","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"German Centre for Cardiovascular Research","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2 3","first":"Catrin","key":"herpichpau","last":"Herpich","name":"Herpich, Catrin","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Stephanie","key":"lehmannpau","last":"Lehmann","name":"Lehmann, Stephanie","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Bastian","key":"kochlikpau","last":"Kochlik","name":"Kochlik, Bastian","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4 5","first":"Maximilian","key":"kleinertpau","last":"Kleinert","locid":"36a8b44b-25a4-4b4b-b047-626c17c3dad1","name":"Kleinert, Maximilian","orcid":"0000-0002-8069-9055","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Susanne","key":"klauspau","last":"Klaus","name":"Klaus, Susanne","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 6","first":"Ursula","key":"müllerwerdanpau","last":"Müller-Werdan","name":"Müller-Werdan, Ursula","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2 3 7","first":"Kristina","key":"normanpau","last":"Norman","name":"Norman, Kristina","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36235718"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/nu14194066","issn":["20726643"],"issue":"19","journal":"Nutrients","paperid":"4066","status":"p","title":"Nutrients","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85139795344"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-a35f71d0-7b86-47a5-b463-1a08078e8db3"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The effect of dextrose or protein ingestion on circulating growth differentiation factor 15 and appetite in older compared to younger women","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-491060","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"The latitudinal diversity gradient (LDG) is one of the most recognized global patterns of species richness exhibited across a wide range of taxa. Numerous hypotheses have been proposed in the past two centuries to explain LDG, but rigorous tests of the drivers of LDGs have been limited by a lack of high-quality global species richness data. Here we produce a high-resolution (0.025 degrees x 0.025 degrees) map of local tree species richness using a global forest inventory database with individual tree information and local biophysical characteristics from similar to 1.3 million sample plots. We then quantify drivers of local tree species richness patterns across latitudes. Generally, annual mean temperature was a dominant predictor of tree species richness, which is most consistent with the metabolic theory of biodiversity (MTB). However, MTB underestimated LDG in the tropics, where high species richness was also moderated by topographic, soil and anthropogenic factors operating at local scales. Given that local landscape variables operate synergistically with bioclimatic factors in shaping the global LDG pattern, we suggest that MTB be extended to account for co-limitation by subordinate drivers.","author_count":254,"contributors":["Liang, Jingjing","Gamarra, Javier G. P.","Picard, Nicolas","Zhou, Mo","Pijanowski, Bryan","Jacobs, Douglass F.","Reich, Peter B.","Crowther, Thomas W.","Nabuurs, Gert-Jan","De-Miguel, Sergio","Fang, Jingyun","Woodall, Christopher W.","Svenning, Jens-Christian","Jucker, Tommaso","Bastin, Jean-Francois","Wiser, Susan K.","Slik, Ferry","Herault, Bruno","Alberti, Giorgio","Keppel, Gunnar","Hengeveld, Geerten M.","Ibisch, Pierre L.","Silva, Carlos A.","Ter Steege, Hans","Peri, Pablo L.","Coomes, David A.","Searle, Eric B.","Von Gadow, Klaus","Jaroszewicz, Bogdan","Abbasi, Akane O.","Abegg, Meinrad","Yao, Yves C. Adou","Aguirre-Gutierrez, Jesus","Zambrano, Angelica M. Almeyda","Altman, Jan","Alvarez-Davila, Esteban","Alvarez-Gonza