st":"Zhu","name":"Zhu, Xiao","rank":245,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"169","first":"Zhi-Xin","key":"zhuzhixinpau","last":"Zhu","name":"Zhu, Zhi-Xin","rank":246,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"45","first":"Irie C.","key":"zobiiriecpau","last":"Zo-Bi","name":"Zo-Bi, Irie C.","rank":247,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"175","first":"Cang","key":"huicangpau","last":"Hui","name":"Hui, Cang","rank":248,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35941205"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41559-022-01831-x","issn":["2397334X"],"issue":"10","journal":"Nature Ecology & Evolution","pages":"1423-1437","publisher":"Nature Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"Nature Ecology & Evolution","volume":"6"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85136829992"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-63683dc0-eadb-4393-a591-aeb444734d85","ku-7ad37a7d-9892-4090-9916-dfc6e7ccba71"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Co-limitation towards lower latitudes shapes global forest diversity gradients","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-085.73-019874","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Age at first sexual intercourse and age at first birth have implications for health and evolutionary fitness. In this genome-wide association study (age at first sexual intercourse, N = 387,338; age at first birth, N = 542,901), we identify 371 single-nucleotide polymorphisms, 11 sex-specific, with a 5–6% polygenic score prediction. Heritability of age at first birth shifted from 9% [CI = 4–14%] for women born in 1940 to 22% [CI = 19–25%] for those born in 1965. Signals are driven by the genetics of reproductive biology and externalising behaviour, with key genes related to follicle stimulating hormone (FSHB), implantation (ESR1), infertility and spermatid differentiation. Our findings suggest that polycystic ovarian syndrome may lead to later age at first birth, linking with infertility. Late age at first birth is associated with parental longevity and reduced incidence of type 2 diabetes and cardiovascular disease. Higher childhood socioeconomic circumstances and those in the highest polygenic score decile (90%+) experience markedly later reproductive onset. Results are relevant for improving teenage and late-life health, understanding longevity and guiding experimentation into mechanisms of infertility.","author_count":50,"contributors":["Mills, Melinda C.","Tropf, Felix C.","Brazel, David M.","van Zuydam, Natalie","Vaez, Ahmad","Agbessi, Mawussé","Ahsan, Habibul","Alves, Isabel","Andiappan, Anand Kumar","Arindrarto, Wibowo","Awadalla, Philip","Battle, Alexis","Beutner, Frank","Jan Bonder, Marc","Boomsma, Dorret I.","Christiansen, Mark W.","Claringbould, Annique","Deelen, Patrick","Esko, Tõnu","Favé, Marie-Julie","Franke, Lude","Frayling, Timothy","Gharib, Sina A.","Gibson, Greg","Heijmans, Bastiaan T.","Hemani, Gibran","Jansen, Rick","Kähönen, Mika","Kalnapenkis, Anette","Kasela, Silva","Kettunen, Johannes","Kim, Yungil","Kirsten, Holger","Krohn, Knut","Kronberg, Jaanika","Kukushkina, Viktorija","Kutalik, Zoltan","Lee, Bernett","Lehtimäki, Terho","Loeffler, Markus","Marigorta, Urko M.","Mei, Hailang","Milani, Lili","Montgomery, Grant W.","Müller-Nurasyid, Martina","Nauck, Matthias","Nivard, Michel G.","Penninx, Brenda W. J. H.","Møllegaard, Stine","Pers, Tune H."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-502058"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corpau":["BIOS Consortium","Human Reproductive Behaviour Consortium","eQTLGen Consortium"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"identification of 000000000371 genetic variants for age at first sex and birth linked to externalising behaviour","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC7612120/pdf/EMS124573.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-502058","identifier":[{"id":"000668823900002","type":"wos"},{"id":"34211149","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC7612120","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85117508270","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-b5ddf72a-e742-4f5a-8c78-d5474563b93d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-A5685C005463A516859579698E3CBA3B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC7612120/pdf/EMS124573.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Sociology, Department of Sociology